WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.338
[energetic string music] ♪

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:06.465
Maile Harris&gt;&gt;
For that brief interval of a song

00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:10.593
the entire world just melts away
and that is what always brings me back

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:17.267
[music continues] ♪

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.687
Nick Deluca&gt;&gt;
Coming into Yale

00:00:18.728 --> 00:00:21.355
I knew there was a Yale Ballroom team,
I emailed over the summer

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:23.565
I showed up to the first few lessons
and from there it's

00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:26.985
pretty much been my
main activity here on campus

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:30.113
As soon as I started dancing with
some of the senior members of the team

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:33.325
I knew that those were the people
I wanted to spend the next four years with

00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:37.078
[upbeat samba music] ♪

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.707
Maile&gt;&gt; There are about 40
members on the team

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:42.543
we're an entirely student run
organization

00:00:42.585 --> 00:00:47.548
we don't have any professional faculty
or any sort of advisor on our team

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:48.883
It's all student run.

00:00:48.925 --> 00:00:51.468
"So you want me to step out?"

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.847
Nick&gt;&gt; In August to about September
that's mostly just practice

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.348
Maile&gt;&gt; That's really a time for all of us
to learn from each other

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.975
"yeah, that works!"

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:00.978
When someone doesn't know
how to do something

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.523
we always know we can go to each other
to be each other's teachers and coaches

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:07.358
"5,6,7,8... 1,2...!"

00:01:07.402 --> 00:01:11.947
There's a huge balancing act that we all try
to juggle as we're going through training

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:16.285
you know you've got a full day of classes
and coming home at the end of the day

00:01:16.285 --> 00:01:19.288
you really are exhausted so it's the
question of

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:23.250
why continue? Why do one more thing
that pushes you further?

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:24.418
"Ok, one more time..."

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:28.255
It's because there's something in you
that connects to the music

00:01:28.297 --> 00:01:31.633
there's something in you
that connects to another person

00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:38.015
and that is what helps you drive
yourself forward in everything else

00:01:38.015 --> 00:01:40.392
when you get to refresh
yourself through dance

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:48.738
[slow ballad music] ♪

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.780
Nick&gt;&gt; In other sports that I've done
I never get the sense that I can stop thinking

00:01:52.822 --> 00:01:57.243
but when we dance typically I don't
remember anything else besides us dancing

00:01:57.285 --> 00:01:59.870
[passionate dance music] ♪
[audience cheers]

00:01:59.912 --> 00:02:03.792
Nick&gt;&gt;
It's also something that we provide

00:02:03.833 --> 00:02:06.210
to the Yale community that they
can all enjoy

00:02:06.252 --> 00:02:09.380
and something new and something that's
not really focused on anymore

00:02:09.422 --> 00:02:13.550
Maile&gt;&gt; You exist entirely in that moment
with the people that you are

00:02:13.592 --> 00:02:16.053
creating with and storytelling with

00:02:16.095 --> 00:02:20.933
That reinforces the kind of community and kind of bond that we share off the dance floor

00:02:20.975 --> 00:02:23.603
because we take off our dance shoes
we put on street shoes

00:02:23.603 --> 00:02:25.020
we don't stop being partners

00:02:25.062 --> 00:02:26.897
Maile&gt;&gt; For the love of dance
Nick&gt;&gt; For the love of dance

00:02:26.938 --> 00:02:31.693
[music ends] ♪
[clapping]

